{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>His soul</b> — the meaning of נפשו is like the pattern of כי נפש כל בשר, דמו בנפשו הוא — and it is that which dies upon the departure of the breath [soul]." "And the meaning of תלין — like תשכב. The sense is that until the day of his death he will be in this world in good. And some say: that this is a hint to the life of his soul, and it will be in good."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:28:32.324382967Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}